{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034775-white-wolf-and-focus-home-interactive-to-release-video-game-adaptation-of-wta","id":1034775,"title":"White Wolf and Focus Home Interactive to release video game adaptation of WtA","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-19T12:22:29-08:00","id":1034775,"title":"White Wolf and Focus Home Interactive to release video game adaptation of WtA","content":"Well, since I didn't see anyone else mentioning this yet, have a link to the official announcement at <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/en/white-wolf-partners-with-focus-home-interactive-for-a-video-game-adaptation-of-the-world-of-darkness-storyteller-game-werewolf-the-apocalypse/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/e...he-apocalypse/</a><br /> <br /> Nice to see the guys downstairs start their revival on the screen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI have long since forsaken mortal blood. It offers me nothing but the stale taste of mayflies. I have partaken of Luna's ever-changing children and dined on the scholars of Magic. I have bled monsters, born and created. No more. Tonight I drink the blood of gods and slake my thirst for another thousand years of night.\u201d","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/312-grunt","name":"Grunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:21:05-08:00","id":1034823,"title":"","content":"Very, very happy about this.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I've been waiting for what seems like forever for another game set in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> After beating Redemption 56 times, Hunter the Reckoning(all 3 of them) 7 times, and Bloodlines around 134 times, we were due for a Werewolf: The Apocalypse videogame.<br /> <br /> Now I hope we don't have to wait much longer or I'm going to rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:27:52-08:00","id":1034830,"title":"","content":"I hope they change the &quot;When will you Rage?&quot; to this forum's present tagline of &quot;how will you Rage?&quot;. That &quot;old school&quot; summary style continues to be not particularly encouraging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:41:32-08:00","id":1034839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034775-white-wolf-and-focus-home-interactive-to-release-video-game-adaptation-of-wta?p=1034830#post1034830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope they change the &quot;When will you Rage?&quot; to this forum's present tagline of &quot;how will you Rage?&quot;. That &quot;old school&quot; summary style continues to be not particularly encouraging.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've always liked the original &quot;When Will You Rage?&quot; tagline. Hope they go with it.<br /> <br /> &quot;How Will You Rage?&quot; is fine, too. Either way, I hope they do WtA justice. I haven't been this excited for a videogame in a long time.<br /> <br /> Wonder if it will come to consoles...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T16:03:18-08:00","id":1034914,"title":"","content":"I like the 'When Will You Rage' line also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar95_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"95\" data-vbnamecard=\"95\">Fat Larry</a>. It is a savage call to arms that feels somewhat ominous and inevitable...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T10:44:20-08:00","id":1035308,"title":"","content":"Very interesting news and hopefully this will come out good and we can rejoice over a splendid version of the World of Darkness. So in short, good to see that Werewolf gets some digital love! Furry eco-terrorists for everybody! (intended as a joke if someone would think otherwise of it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:48:59-08:00","id":1035347,"title":"","content":"Okay, as someone who has played both vampire games, some thoughts;<br /> <br /> It better be a bioware style rpg. Because WtA is about the pack and not a lone wolf. VtMB was a great game, but I think what hurt it was that you never truly had a chance to have true allies. Also, Redemption's cast was pretty silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:58:58-08:00","id":1035352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034775-white-wolf-and-focus-home-interactive-to-release-video-game-adaptation-of-wta?p=1035347#post1035347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It better be a bioware style rpg. Because WtA is about the pack and not a lone wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>A friend and I were just talking about that this morning! &quot;Think it'll be multiplayer?&quot; // 'Maybe, but it as least needs to be multi-character. It's Werewolf! Gotta have a pack!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:18:09-08:00","id":1035402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034775-white-wolf-and-focus-home-interactive-to-release-video-game-adaptation-of-wta?p=1035347#post1035347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, as someone who has played both vampire games, some thoughts;<br /> <br /> <b>It better be a bioware style rpg</b>. Because WtA is about the pack and not a lone wolf. VtMB was a great game, but I think what hurt it was that you never truly had a chance to have true allies. Also, Redemption's cast was pretty silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe if it were old Bioware. New Bioware is terrible.<br /> <br /> And the cast of Redemption was fantastic. It had the only fish-Malk I've ever liked. Pink and Erik were great, as were Lily and Sam the Nossie. I loved Redemption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:22:18-08:00","id":1035407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034775-white-wolf-and-focus-home-interactive-to-release-video-game-adaptation-of-wta?p=1035402#post1035402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe if it were old Bioware. New Bioware is terrible.<br /> <br /> And the cast of Redemption was fantastic. It had the only fish-Malk I've ever liked. <b>Pink </b>and Erik were great, as were Lily and Sam the Nossie. I loved Redemption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pink 'as a mite stupid name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:25:34-08:00","id":1035412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034775-white-wolf-and-focus-home-interactive-to-release-video-game-adaptation-of-wta?p=1035407#post1035407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pink 'as a mite stupid name.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was kinda the point. : )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T19:13:00-08:00","id":1035583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034775-white-wolf-and-focus-home-interactive-to-release-video-game-adaptation-of-wta?p=1035347#post1035347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, as someone who has played both vampire games, some thoughts;<br /> <br /> It better be a bioware style rpg. Because WtA is about the pack and not a lone wolf. VtMB was a great game, but I think what hurt it was that you never truly had a chance to have true allies. Also, Redemption's cast was pretty silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>In regards to a pack I agree. The ability to get a pack together should be fairly important, but to be honest I'd rather have a solo werewolf than struggling with a pack of imbecile AI.<br /> <br /> In regards to Bloodlines I kind of liked how you were always on your own. It drove home the point that vampires tend to be loners and that they seldom forge healthy, to my understanding of the term, relations with others. Running around with half a dozen best-friends-forever characters would kind of ruin this point. And no, I've never played Redemption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T19:33:07-08:00","id":1035588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034775-white-wolf-and-focus-home-interactive-to-release-video-game-adaptation-of-wta?p=1035583#post1035583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In regards to a pack I agree. The ability to get a pack together should be fairly important, but to be honest I'd rather have a solo werewolf than struggling with a pack of imbecile AI.<br /> <br /> In regards to Bloodlines I kind of liked how you were always on your own. It drove home the point that vampires tend to be loners and that they seldom forge healthy, to my understanding of the term, relations with others. Running around with half a dozen best-friends-forever characters would kind of ruin this point. And no, I've never played Redemption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not do something similar to the team mechanics in GTA V? be able to switch between packmates on the fly, and maybe have Kinfolk fill the same role that the hired hackers, gunman and drivers (as well as the various hired help in Payday 2 heists) did as basically filling defined jobs on the major quests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T19:39:55-08:00","id":1035590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034775-white-wolf-and-focus-home-interactive-to-release-video-game-adaptation-of-wta?p=1035583#post1035583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In regards to a pack I agree. The ability to get a pack together should be fairly important, but to be honest I'd rather have a solo werewolf than struggling with a pack of imbecile AI.<br /> <br /> In regards to Bloodlines I kind of liked how you were always on your own. It drove home the point that vampires tend to be loners and that they seldom forge healthy, to my understanding of the term, relations with others. Running around with half a dozen best-friends-forever characters would kind of ruin this point. And no, I've never played Redemption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, never had an issue with DAIs AI, after I found what settings worked for me.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines has that, I agree. It is the best intro to WoD in video game form so far. But only an intro, because a huge part of VtM is also dealing with your allies politically and socially. Bloodlines limits you to only being a delivery boy.<br /> <br /> As for Redemption's cast, there ARE some good characters. Anezka is awesome and really won over me by the end with her schemes. But Christoff is a bit ehh, Wilhelm is okay. And yes, Sam and Lily are actually good characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T20:46:18-08:00","id":1035607,"title":"","content":"Dragon Age Inquisition's biggest issue was leaning on MMO style grinding for resources and a world much bigger and harder to traverse than it needed to be. AI was never a huge issue for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T21:08:06-08:00","id":1035609,"title":"","content":"I'd agree that a tactical-heavy, old school rpg would be the best for WtA. I recently finished Shadowrun Returns and currently playing through Dragonfall. Those games were a big, big positive surprise. <br /> <br /> Bloodlines was very good (well, aside from the never-ending dungeon crawls in the sewers at the end), but I prefer traditional, team-based rpgs and in game, like Werewolf, where pact teamwork and dynamics are extremely important, that's especially adequate.<br /> <br /> I liked Redemption too, it was fun, the characters were fun, but again, some dungeons were just too long to my tastes. That and I prefer isometric, 2d rpgs, with beautifully drawn landscapes. Yeah, I'm an old Bioware fan and I played BG and IWD many times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, fingers crossing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T21:52:20-08:00","id":1035623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034775-white-wolf-and-focus-home-interactive-to-release-video-game-adaptation-of-wta?p=1035609#post1035609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd agree that a tactical-heavy, old school rpg would be the best for WtA.<b> I recently finished Shadowrun Returns and currently playing through Dragonfall.</b> Those games were a big, big positive surprise.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines was very good (well, aside from the never-ending dungeon crawls in the sewers at the end), but I prefer traditional, team-based rpgs and in game, like Werewolf, where pact teamwork and dynamics are extremely important, that's especially adequate.<br /> <br /> I liked Redemption too, it was fun, the characters were fun, but again, some dungeons were just too long to my tastes. That and I prefer isometric, 2d rpgs, with beautifully drawn landscapes. Yeah, I'm an old Bioware fan and I played BG and IWD many times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, fingers crossing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just finished Shadowrun Returns ten minutes ago. : ) Loved it. And would love to see the Werewolf the Apocalypse video game follow in its footsteps. I'm about to start Shadowrun Hong Kong, too. <br /> <br /> With that said, we should know more at Focus Home Interactive's next event which is Feb 1st, I believe. So...soon!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T09:57:57-08:00","id":1035733,"title":"","content":"I'm really excited for this because Werewolf is my favourite cWoD setting. I agree that it would likely have to be like a classic Bioware RPG, although likely with more flowing movement mechanics (because of course I'm going to be using lupus form to run around the map if possible). I don't have a problem with more action-oriented combat if the teammate AI is alright, but I don't expect it's going to be particularly brilliant, so if we can get a pack-based more traditional RPG I'll be 100% sold.<br /> <br /> I am worried about what they're going to do with the 5 forms though, because I have a feeling it might boil down to Homid=talking scenes and being stealthy, Crinos=combat, without any of the others being important/playable. Which would be a shame, especially if the game decides to include lupus characters as well as homids and metis.<br /> <br /> Hello to this subforum by the way, because I don't think I've posted here before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T10:17:00-08:00","id":1035739,"title":"","content":"At this point, I'd enjoy an 8 bit sprite Werewolf game. That being said, I liked the playstyle of the DragonAge games and I could see that lending itself well to running a small pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T10:28:09-08:00","id":1035745,"title":"","content":"I really hope it isn't a braindead beat-em-up game. I want to be able to interact with spirits and deal with challenges between septs as much as I want to splatter mockeries into Wyrm-paste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:33:48-08:00","id":1035791,"title":"","content":"I definitely hope it has some hard roleplaying elements - having conversations with NPCs, lore dumps, making important choices, etc. I don't mind it being combat heavy, but I'd be kind of sad if it were only combat focused. Seeing as how this game is going to be coming from Focus Home Interactive which has helped produce some good games like the Walking Dead and The Wolf Among Us so I'm fairly confident that they'll be able to give us something more than just brainless combat.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* Oh, but now that I look closer, it's the actual developer is studio Cyanide. To date they have made average game after average game. Lots of good bicycle riding games if you're into those, but nearly everything else they have produced has been fairly unpolished and buggy at best. They haven't had much in the way of successful RPGs and pretty much nothing they have released can be considered &quot;great.&quot; They're almost like a textbook example of a &quot;slightly below average game studio with a couple of moderate successes.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's possible that lightning will strike and this Werewolf game will be great, but as of right now I'm expecting that the game we get will be fairly buggy, will not have anywhere near as much stuff as we actually want, and will ultimately have some really cool ideas that just never really get explored in a way that will make me happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-21-2017, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T15:59:11-08:00","id":1035879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034775-white-wolf-and-focus-home-interactive-to-release-video-game-adaptation-of-wta?p=1035791#post1035791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely hope it has some hard roleplaying elements - having conversations with NPCs, lore dumps, making important choices, etc. I don't mind it being combat heavy, but I'd be kind of sad if it were only combat focused. Seeing as how this game is going to be coming from Focus Home Interactive which has helped produce some good games like the Walking Dead and The Wolf Among Us so I'm fairly confident that they'll be able to give us something more than just brainless combat.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* Oh, but now that I look closer, it's the actual developer is studio Cyanide. To date they have made average game after average game. Lots of good bicycle riding games if you're into those, but nearly everything else they have produced has been fairly unpolished and buggy at best. They haven't had much in the way of successful RPGs and pretty much nothing they have released can be considered &quot;great.&quot; They're almost like a textbook example of a &quot;slightly below average game studio with a couple of moderate successes.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's possible that lightning will strike and this Werewolf game will be great, but as of right now I'm expecting that the game we get will be fairly buggy, will not have anywhere near as much stuff as we actually want, and will ultimately have some really cool ideas that just never really get explored in a way that will make me happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the Steam ratings of their games, the games Cyanide developed that were published by Focus Home are actually pretty good, one can only assume that Focus Home is more involved with the process than simply being the publisher and thus, the Cyanide adaption of Werewolf might actually be pretty good as well..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T16:49:38-08:00","id":1035892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034775-white-wolf-and-focus-home-interactive-to-release-video-game-adaptation-of-wta?p=1035791#post1035791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible that lightning will strike and this Werewolf game will be great, but as of right now I'm expecting that the game we get will be fairly buggy, will not have anywhere near as much stuff as we actually want, and will ultimately have some really cool ideas that just never really get explored in a way that will make me happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hot takes aside, Styx: Master of Shadows is actually pretty damn good. I wouldn't worry about this game just yet. I'm sure WW knows they have to hit it out the park first go around.<br /> <br /> And an RPG would be best, but dammit I'd also take ANOTHER Werewolf game in the vein of Streets of Rage 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T16:51:47-08:00","id":1035893,"title":"","content":"They just announced new Vampire, Wraith, and Mage mobile video games are coming as well. VERY excited about this.<br /> <br /> I wasn't expecting something gigantic off the bat. They need to get their feet wet first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":